+# Consulted Broadcom sources
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 using live network research.
+
+- **Guidelines to upgrade to VCF 5.2.x with Async Patched vCenters (7.0U3T, 8.0U2E, 8.0U3D)** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/381567 — Identifies the back-in-time incompatibility for VCF 4.5.2 with vCenter 7.0 U3t and calls for a customized 8.0 U3d-or-later vCenter target.
+- **VCF 5.0.x is not a supported upgrade path if you are running VCF 4.5.2 version** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/313502 — Confirms that 4.5.2 to either 5.0.x release is not a supported lifecycle transition.
+- **Applying individual product updates to VMware Cloud Foundation environments using Async Patch** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/344935 — Provides the VCF component compatibility and minimum-target data used to cross-check the pinned component choices.
+- **Upgrade plan in SDDC manager shows “Cannot upgrade to VCF version 5.2.1.0 for domain &lt;domain_id&gt; in a compatible way: not upgradable:”** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/405807 — Describes the same back-in-time restriction against the default VCF 5.2.1 vCenter/ESXi payloads for late 7.0 U3 patches.
